# The representation search's winner, crossed with the vector learners.
#
# lengthfree_geom = step mean with step length regressed out of every position,
# plus 20 scale-free geometry features describing the shape of the step's token
# cloud. 4,116 dimensions on Qwen3-8B-Base.
#
# Why this cell list exists. Under a deterministic ridge probe on the screen's
# sample, measured against the same probe on the same rows:
#
#   step mean                          0.7470
#   step mean, length removed          0.7282   removing length ALONE costs
#   the 20 geometry features alone     0.5182   they are useless ALONE
#   both together                      0.7897   and win 1000/1000 paired resamples
#
# The gain is an interaction, not two additions. Length is a cue that works in
# training (PRM800K steps average 38.8 tokens) and misleads at test time
# (ProcessBench steps run 79.7 and 118.6), so removing it and handing back only
# the scale-free part of what it stood in for beats both keeping it and dropping
# it. It is also the best representation inside length strata (0.7377), where a
# token count scores 0.5097, so it is not winning on the shortcut.
#
# The screen predicted the full metric at Spearman 0.934 over 31 cells, which is
# a good enough reason to spend grid time here and not a substitute for it. This
# run is what decides whether the result holds on calib-20 F1.
#
# step_mean is included at the same three learners so the comparison is paired
# within this job rather than read across runs.

lengthfree_geom linear
lengthfree_geom mlp:h1024
lengthfree_geom mlp:h1024x2
step_mean linear
step_mean mlp:h1024
step_mean mlp:h1024x2
